---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: nested-legacy-meta
root: true
rules:
  - id: nested-legacy-rule
    class: ask
    when: { write: "leaf.md" }
    route-to: { dest: docs/plans }
---
Parity fixture 2 (Task 6 / B2) — legacy nested `.epr-meta` flat file (not directory-form),
marked `root: true` so the cascade terminates here without walking above this fixture.
Shared corpus for `.claude/scripts/_lib/__tests__/epr_meta_cascade_test.py` and
`elohim/eprfs/eprfs-meta/tests/parity.rs`. Do not hand-edit one side without the other.

The `when: { write: "leaf.md" }` scope is deliberate: `sub/leaf.md` is a fictional, never-created
target path used only to resolve the cascade in the parity tests. Scoping the rule to that literal
filename keeps this fixture's `ask` rule from ever firing on this manifest's own creation/edits when
committed — `.epr-meta` files are live governance input to the real git/PreToolUse hooks, not inert
test data.
